  "note": "Verda runs (runs/*@verda), final pipeline. Cold = ledger emptied before the run (real entries backed up to context/ledger.cold-backup.jsonl and restored after). After each cold case the oracle answers its questions into the ledger; warm re-runs every case with that ledger. repeat_questions = warm questions whose area and wording match an answered one (should be 0). bait_false_alarms = non-baseline verified findings at the bait's planted lines. ledger_citations = lens findings withdrawn as deliberate per a ledger entry. Cold->warm answers come from `bench-oracle (simulated human)`: a script that answers from the bench ground truth (bait conventions, else the option closest to the requirement). It is not a person."
